cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "reefunit: wave-driven sliding, ratcheting and overturning of coral transplant units"
abstract: >-
  An idealized, uncalibrated model of the mechanical failure of coral
  transplant units under waves, currents and internal solitary waves.  A
  unit is a planar rigid body on a rigid bed with two unilateral
  frictional contacts, loaded through a Morison description of near-bed
  wave kinematics.  The library provides closed-form stability
  thresholds, a Moreau-Jean time-stepper with two independent
  event-driven reference solvers, and the figure and report pipeline of
  the accompanying paper.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sandyherho/reefunit"
keywords:
  - coral restoration
  - transplant unit stability
  - nonsmooth dynamics
  - rocking block
  - internal solitary wave
  - Indonesia
